The driver supports the Acer Labs M5229 IDE controllers, and pro‐
vides the interface with the hardware for the driver.  The 0x0002
flag  forces  the driver to disable DMA on chipsets for which DMA
would normally be enabled.  This can be used as a debugging  aid,
or  to  work around problems where the IDE controller is wired up
to the system incorrectly.  The timings used for the PIO and  DMA
modes  for  controllers listed above are for a PCI bus running at
30 or 33 MHz.  This driver may not work properly  on  overclocked
systems.
